{"book":28,"chapter":14,"context":{"chapter":14,"title":"Return, and Be Healed","summary":"Hosea's final call invites Israel to return with honest words; God promises to heal their backsliding, love them freely and make them flourish like a lily and the cedars of Lebanon.","background":"The book ends with a scripted prayer of repentance (vv. 2–3) that renounces the very things Israel trusted: Assyria, war horses and handmade idols. The images of dew, lily, olive tree and Lebanon's fragrance reverse the drought and barrenness threatened earlier. The final verse invites readers to take its lessons to heart.","customs":[{"term":"Calves of our lips","verses":"14:2","note":"Instead of offering bulls, Israel will offer words of praise. The ancient Greek version reads 'fruit of our lips,' echoed in Hebrews 13:15."}],"watchFor":["'Take with you words' (v. 2).","'I will heal their backsliding, I will love them freely' (v. 4).","Dew, the gift Baal was thought to give, comes from God (v. 5)."],"connections":["Hebrews 13:15","Jeremiah 3:22","Psalms 1:6"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["שׁוּבָה","shuvah","H7725","HVqv2ms/Sh","return !"],["יִשְׂרָאֵל","yisra'el","H3478","HNpl","O Israel"],["עַד","'ad","H5704","HR","to"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֱלֹהֶיךָ","'eloheikha","H430","HNcmpc/Sp2ms","God your"],["כִּי","ki","H3588","HTc","for"],["כָשַׁלְתָּ","khashalta","H3782","HVqp2ms","you have stumbled"],["בַּעֲוֹנֶךָ","ba'avonekha","H5771","HR/Ncmsc/Sp2ms","on iniquity your"]],"x":[[28006001,28006001,18],[29002012,29002013,18],[28012006,28012006,13],[14030006,14030009,10],[38001003,38001004,9],[23055006,23055007,7],[24004001,24004001,7],[44026018,44026020,7],[28013009,28013009,5],[24003012,24003014,4]],"xn":12},"2":{"w":[["קְחוּ","kechu","H3947","HVqv2mp","take"],["עִמָּכֶם","'imakhem","H5973","HRd/Sp2mp","with you"],["דְּבָרִים","devarim","H1697","HNcmpa","words"],["וְשׁוּבוּ","veshuvu","H7725","HC/Vqv2mp","and return"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","